# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  UNSENT — main story: arrival, nights, Lantern Night, endings
#
#  Syntax:  === node.id            start a node
#           speaker[expr]: text    a line  (n: = narration)
#           * text -> node         a choice ( * [if cond] text -> node )
#           -> node                jump      ( [if cond] -> node )
#           ~ command args         run a command
#           [if cond] <anything>   conditional instruction
#           $flag in conditions reads a story flag
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

=== intro.harbor
~ set intro_done
~ letterbox on
~ wait 0.6
n: *In Hushwater, the sun has been setting for seventeen years.*
n: *Nobody remembers quite when the dusk stopped moving. Only that it did — on the night of the Long Storm — and that the town clock stopped with it, at eight minutes to midnight.*
n: *The evening ferry is the only boat that still comes. Tonight, it brings one passenger.*
~ npc bram face left
bram[happy]: Hushwater! Last stop, only stop. Mind the gulls, mind the gap, and mind the dusk — it gets into your coat.
wren: Is it always this... orange?
bram[happy]: Orange, violet, a bit of peach on Sundays. You'll stop noticing. Or you won't, and you'll go a little strange, like the rest of us.
bram: You'll be the new night clerk. Odile said to send you straight up. Post office is the crooked building at the end of the quay — use the back door, she can't abide the front bell.
bram[thinking]: Off you go then, little bird. Bram Calloway, captain of the Morning Lark, at your service. Lost and Found's my shed, if you ever lose anything. Most people do, here.
~ set met_bram
~ letterbox off
~ objective "Find the post office at the end of the quay."

=== po.first_visit
~ set met_odile
~ letterbox on
~ npc odile face left
odile: You're late.
wren: The ferry was—
odile[happy]: I know, dear, I'm teasing. The ferry is never late. It's simply never on time. Come in, come in, let me look at you.
odile[thinking]: Hm. Good eyes. I can tell, even with mine. A kind heart is harder to see. We'll find out.
odile: I'm Odile Vance, postmistress. This is the Hushwater Post Office — or, as it says on the forms nobody fills in, the *Office of Unsent Letters.*
* What's an unsent letter? -> po.first_visit.what
* I don't actually remember applying for this job. -> po.first_visit.apply

=== po.first_visit.what
odile: Every letter somebody wrote and couldn't bring themselves to post. The apology in the drawer. The confession folded into a library book. The "I'm sorry" that went into the fire.
odile: They don't vanish, you know. Words don't. They come here.
-> po.first_visit.chute

=== po.first_visit.apply
odile[surprised]: Don't you? Your letter of application was very persuasive. Lovely handwriting.
wren: I don't remember writing one.
odile[happy]: Then you'll fit in beautifully. Nobody in Hushwater remembers anything properly. It's the dusk.
-> po.first_visit.chute

=== po.first_visit.chute
odile: That brass monster behind me is the Chute. Unsent letters arrive through it, when they're ready to be delivered. It doesn't connect to anything. I've checked. Twice.
odile[sad]: My eyes aren't what they were. The handwriting swims. And lately the Chute has been... odd.
wren: Odd how?
odile[thinking]: Some of the letters are dated wrong. Years wrong. Years that haven't *happened* yet.
~ sfx chute
~ shake 0.5
n: *The Chute shudders. Somewhere inside it, something rattles downward — and a little bell rings, bright as a spoon against glass.*
odile[happy]: Ah. Your first. How punctual. Go on, then — it's in the basket.
~ arrive blue_door
~ letterbox off
~ objective "Collect the letter from the Chute."

=== po.after_first_letter
~ set tutorial_done
~ letterbox on
odile: Well? Who's it for?
wren: There's no name. Just a "T." at the bottom.
odile: There never is a name, dear. That would make it a letter, and these are *unsent* letters. You'll have to find out who it was written for.
odile: Read it closely — tap the words that matter, and they'll go in your notes. Turn the envelope over. Then go out and ask people. Hushwater is small. Everyone in it is somebody's clue.
odile[thinking]: And Wren — never deliver on a guess. You'll need at least two good reasons before you hand a letter to anyone. A letter in the wrong hands is worse than no letter at all.
odile: The front door goes out to Lantern Square. The back door, to the harbour. If you get stuck, come and ask me. I'm half blind, not half witted.
~ letterbox off
~ objective "Find who 'The Light Above the Blue Door' was written for."

# ─── Nights ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

=== night.2.start
~ letterbox on
odile: Up you get, sleepyhead. The Chute's been rattling since the clock didn't strike three.
odile[thinking]: Four letters. *Four.* And two of them are dated twenty years from now — I can feel it from here. Future letters are always colder. Like coins from someone else's pocket.
odile: The cliff path's open, too. Tobias won't thank you for visiting. Visit anyway.
~ letterbox off
~ objective "Collect tonight's letters from the Chute."

=== night.3.start
~ letterbox on
odile: Two more tonight. One smells of the sea. One smells of bread.
odile[sad]: And tomorrow's Lantern Night. I always dread the post the night before Lantern Night.
~ letterbox off
~ objective "Collect tonight's letters from the Chute."

=== night.4.start
-> po.lantern_start

=== po.lantern_start
~ set lantern_started
~ letterbox on
n: *Lantern Night. The anniversary of the Long Storm.*
n: *Rain hammers the windows. The barometer in the hall has fallen so far it has stopped pretending.*
odile: There you are. Here — take this. A paper lantern. Everyone lights one at the harbour tonight, for whoever they've lost.
odile[thinking]: Or for whoever they're going to lose. I've always thought that the braver kind.
~ item paper_lantern
[if $tobias_knows] -> po.lantern_start.tobias
odile: Tobias will be up his tower, as always. Bram's bringing the 8:15 across in this weather, Lord help him.
odile: Go on down to the harbour when you're ready. And deliver what you can before the night is out. Whatever's still in your satchel by midnight... well. Some letters stay unsent.
~ letterbox off
~ objective "Lantern Night. Go down to the harbour before 11:40."

=== po.lantern_start.tobias
odile[shy]: And... Tobias has sent word, through Bram. Eleven-forty. The end of the pier.
odile[happy]: Forty-one years late, and the man is still *punctual*.
odile[sad]: Which means someone else has to mind that lamp tonight.
[if not $read_ps_1140] odile[thinking]: There's a letter in the Chute for you, by the way. It's in my handwriting. I didn't write it. Yet.
odile: Don't let it go dark, Wren. Not tonight.
~ letterbox off
~ objective "Lantern Night. Make sure someone is in the lamp room at 11:40."

# ─── Lantern Night finale ────────────────────────────────────────────

=== finale.lamp_room
[if lamp_keeper() == "june"] -> finale.lamp_room.june
[if lamp_keeper() == "tobias"] -> finale.lamp_room.tobias
-> finale.lamp_room.self

=== finale.lamp_room.self
~ letterbox on
~ ambience storm
n: *Wind screams through the gallery glass. Far below, the sea throws itself against the Teeth.*
n: *The automatic lamp hums in its brass box — steady, smug.*
~ wait 0.8
~ flash
~ sfx thunder
~ shake 1.0
n: *Lightning strikes the rod. Every gear in the box seizes at once with a sound like a bitten-off word.*
~ set auto_lamp_failed
~ set lamp_sequence 1
~ sfx lamp_die
~ refresh
n: *The light goes out. It is 11:40.*
[if $knows_lamp_order] wren: Oil. Wick. Flame. In that order — that's what Tobias said.
[if not $knows_lamp_order] wren: There has to be an order to this. Think.
~ letterbox off
~ objective "Light the lamp before the Morning Lark reaches the Teeth."

=== lamp.valve
[if $lamp_sequence == 1] -> lamp.valve.ok
n: *The valve is open. Oil gurgles in the reservoir, sharp and green-smelling.*

=== lamp.valve.ok
~ sfx valve
n: *You crank the brass valve. Oil gurgles up into the reservoir.*
~ set lamp_sequence 2

=== lamp.wick
[if $lamp_sequence == 1] wren: The wick's bone dry. It needs oil first.
[if $lamp_sequence == 2] -> lamp.wick.ok
[if $lamp_sequence == 3] n: *The wick is trimmed square and dark with oil.*

=== lamp.wick.ok
~ sfx snip
n: *You trim the charred wick square with the little scissors hanging on their nail. It drinks the oil.*
~ set lamp_sequence 3

=== lamp.match
[if $lamp_sequence < 3] wren: Not yet. Oil, wick, then flame — or I'll lose my eyebrows.
[if $lamp_sequence == 3] -> lamp.ignite

=== lamp.ignite
~ letterbox on
~ sfx match
n: *The first match blows out. The second snaps in half. The third—*
~ sfx ignite
~ set lamp_sequence 4
~ set lamp_lit
~ set lamp_resolved
~ set lit_by_wren
~ refresh
~ music hope
n: *The wick catches. The great lens drinks the flame and throws it, a thousand times brighter, out across the black water.*
n: *And far out in the storm, a small light on the water turns toward it — the Morning Lark, finding her way home.*
~ wait 1.0
-> finale.go_harbor

=== finale.lamp_room.june
~ letterbox on
n: *June is at the lamp. Her yellow coat hangs on a hook; her sleeves are rolled up like her mother's.*
june[happy]: Wren! Isn't it awful out there? I love it. Grandpa showed me everything. Oil, wick, flame. I've got it.
~ wait 0.6
~ flash
~ sfx thunder
~ shake 1.0
n: *Lightning strikes the rod. The automatic lamp's gears seize with a grinding shriek. The light dies.*
~ sfx lamp_die
june[surprised]: Eleven-forty — oh, you *stupid* box—
n: *But her hands are already moving. Valve. Scissors. Match.*
~ sfx ignite
~ set lamp_lit
~ set lamp_resolved
~ refresh
~ music hope
n: *The flame catches. The lens blazes. The beam swings out across the black water — and far out in the storm, the Morning Lark turns toward it.*
june[happy]: Whole heart. Whole heart, whole heart.
june: Go on down to the harbour. I've got this. I've *got* this.
-> finale.go_harbor

=== finale.lamp_room.tobias
~ letterbox on
n: *Tobias stands at the lamp the way he has every night for fifty years — as if the light might bolt if he looked away.*
tobias: Lantern Night. Hm. Come to watch an old man work?
~ wait 0.6
~ flash
~ sfx thunder
~ shake 1.0
n: *At 11:40 the lightning comes. The automatic lamp dies with a shriek of gears — but Tobias's hand is already on the valve. He doesn't even look up.*
~ sfx ignite
~ set lamp_lit
~ set lamp_resolved
~ refresh
tobias: Fifty years. Never missed but the once.
n: *Far out in the storm, the Morning Lark turns toward the light.*
tobias: Go down to the harbour, clerk. Watch them come in. That's the best part. I never get to see it.
-> finale.go_harbor

=== finale.go_harbor
~ letterbox off
~ fade out 1.2
~ set finale
~ goto_location harbor finale
~ run finale.harbor

=== hb.pier_end
[if $lantern_night and not $lamp_resolved] -> finale.pier_wait
[if $lantern_night] n: *The end of the pier. The rain has softened. The lighthouse beam sweeps the water, slow and steady.*
[if $lantern_night] -> END
n: *The very end of the pier. Below, the water slaps lazily at the pilings. Ahead: the sea, the dusk, and the thin gold line where the sun should be.*
[if held("lamp_lit") or delivered("lamp_lit") != ""] n: *"If the lighthouse stays dark, I'll be waiting at the end of the pier."* This is where she waited.
~ clue c2_pier

=== finale.pier_wait
n: *It's almost 11:40. The lighthouse beam swings overhead through the rain — steady, for now.*
[if lamp_keeper() == "nobody" and $read_ps_1140] wren: The letter said the lamp fails at 11:40. Someone has to be up there.
* Wait here at the end of the pier. -> finale.pier_wait.go
* Not yet. -> END

=== finale.pier_wait.go
[if lamp_keeper() == "nobody"] -> finale.pier_dark
-> finale.pier_light

=== finale.pier_dark
~ set finale
~ letterbox on
~ wait 0.6
~ flash
~ sfx thunder
~ shake 1.0
n: *At 11:40, lightning splits the sky above the cliff. The lighthouse beam stutters — once, twice — and goes out.*
~ sfx lamp_die
n: *There is no one in the lamp room. You know it with a sick, sinking certainty.*
~ set lamp_failed
~ set lamp_resolved
~ refresh
-> finale.harbor

=== finale.pier_light
~ set finale
~ letterbox on
~ wait 0.6
~ flash
~ sfx thunder
~ shake 1.0
n: *At 11:40, lightning splits the sky above the cliff. The beam stutters, gutters—*
n: *—and blazes back, brighter than before. Somebody up there knew exactly what to do.*
~ set lamp_lit
~ set lamp_resolved
~ refresh
-> finale.harbor

=== finale.harbor
~ letterbox on
~ music lantern
~ refresh
n: *The harbour is full of people and paper lanterns, bobbing in the rain like a flock of small, stubborn moons.*
[if $lamp_lit] -> finale.harbor.ferry
-> finale.harbor.noferry

=== finale.harbor.noferry
n: *Out on the black water, a small light wavers... turns... and turns away, back toward Port Ardent. The Morning Lark won't risk the Teeth in the dark.*
[if $reply_posted] mari[sad]: He'd have been on it. I know he would.
-> finale.reunion

=== finale.harbor.ferry
~ sfx horn
n: *Out of the dark comes the Morning Lark — rolling, battered, her running lights blazing — following the beam home.*
~ set ferry_home
[if $reply_posted] -> finale.theo
-> finale.reunion

=== finale.theo
~ npc theo show 1180 990
~ npc theo face right
n: *A big man in a dock jacket is first down the gangplank before it's even tied. He stands on the quay in the rain and looks up the lane, toward a lamp above a blue door.*
theo[sad]: Mari?
mari[surprised]: ...Theo?
n: *Mari drops her lantern, or her umbrella, or both. Nobody is entirely sure afterwards, because nobody was looking at anything except the two of them.*
mari[sad]: You *idiot*. You beautiful idiot. Twelve years—
theo[sad]: I saw the light. You left the light on.
mari[happy]: I *re-lit* the light. There's a difference. Come here.
~ set theo_home
-> finale.reunion

=== finale.reunion
[if $tobias_knows and lamp_keeper() != "tobias"] -> finale.pier_couple
-> finale.lanterns

=== finale.pier_couple
n: *At the very end of the pier, under one umbrella, an old man and an old woman stand side by side, looking up at a lighthouse.*
[if $lamp_lit] odile[happy]: It's lit, you know. You're meant to be up there.
[if $lamp_lit] tobias: Someone else has the lamp tonight. I had a question to answer.
[if not $lamp_lit] odile[sad]: It's dark, Tobias. It's dark—
[if not $lamp_lit] tobias[sad]: I know. I know. I'm here anyway.
tobias: Forty-one years late. Hm. I'm sorry, Odile.
odile[happy]: Don't be. You were always going to be late. I simply didn't expect it to be by quite so much.
~ set reunited
-> finale.lanterns

=== finale.lanterns
~ lanterns
n: *All along the quay, people light their paper lanterns and let them go. They rise into the rain, wobbling, and do not go out.*
* Light your own lantern. -> finale.mylantern

=== finale.mylantern
~ take paper_lantern
~ sfx lantern
n: *You write a name on yours. You aren't sure whose it is until it's written.*
n: *It rises with the others.*
[if $clock_running] -> finale.midnight
-> finale.judgement

=== finale.midnight
~ sfx clock_chime
n: *Across the town, for the first time in seventeen years, the clock tower strikes midnight.*
-> finale.judgement

=== finale.judgement
~ letterbox off
~ judge

# ─── Endings ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

=== ending.dawn
~ letterbox on
~ music dawn
~ mood dawn 14
n: *The storm thins. The rain softens to mist. And along the edge of the sea, the thin gold line that has not moved in seventeen years...*
~ wait 2.5
n: *...moves.*
~ wait 2.0
n: *It brightens. It swells. It spills over the water like milk from a tipped jug.*
[if $june_path != "stay"] june[surprised]: Is that — Mum — is that—
[if $june_path == "stay"] n: *High on the cliff, at the top of a hundred and twelve stairs, a girl in a yellow coat is the first person in Hushwater to see it.*
n: *For the first time in seventeen years, the sun rises over Hushwater.*
~ wait 2.0
odile: Wren. Dear. There's a letter for you. It came through the Chute a minute ago — Postscript brought it down in his mouth, the little horror.
odile[thinking]: It's addressed to "the Night Clerk, on the morning after Lantern Night." Which is a ridiculous thing to write on an envelope. And yet.
~ letterbox off
~ read final_dawn
~ letterbox on
-> ending.choice

=== ending.choice
odile: Well? What will you do now?
* Stay. Learn the Chute. Keep the Office of Unsent Letters. -> ending.stay
* [if has_item("ferry_ticket")] Take June's ticket. Ride the 6:10 into the sunrise. -> ending.go

=== ending.stay
wren: I think I'll stay. Someone has to answer the Chute.
odile[happy]: Fifty years, it'll be. Fifty years of other people's hearts in your satchel. It's a terrible job.
odile[happy]: You'll love it.
~ ending first_light

=== ending.go
wren: June gave me her ticket. I think... I'd like to see where the sun goes, after it rises.
odile[sad]: Ah. Well. A wren is a bird, after all.
odile[happy]: Go on, then. The Chute will find someone. It found you. Write to me — properly. *Sent.*
~ ending morning_ferry

=== ending.dusk
~ letterbox on
~ music sad
n: *The storm passes, the way storms do. The rain stops. The lanterns drift out to sea, one by one, and go out.*
n: *And the thin gold line at the edge of the world stays exactly where it has always been.*
odile[sad]: Not this year, then.
odile: Come on, dear. There's a letter for you. It came through the Chute while we were all out. It's in your handwriting, if you can believe it.
~ letterbox off
~ read final_dusk
~ ending long_dusk
